'<!-- Section properties of a right triangle: area, centroid offsets, $I_x$, $I_y$, section moduli and radii of gyration in closed form. -->
'<h1>Geometrical Properties of Right Triangle</h1>
'<div style="max-width:120mm"><img style="height:127pt;" alt="right-triangle.png" class="side" src="../../Images/mechanics/sections/right-triangle.png"></div>
'Side lengths
#UI 'Leg -'a = 2m', Leg -'b = 1m
'Area
A = a*b/2
'Perimeter
P = a + b + sqr(a^2 + b^2)
'Centroid
y_c = a/3
z_c = b/3
'Second moments of area
I_y = a*b^3/36
I_z = a^3*b/36
I_yz = -(a^2*b^2)/72'</p>
'Principal area moments
I_1 = (I_y + I_z)/2 + sqrt((I_y - I_z)^2/4 + I_yz^2)
I_2 = (I_y + I_z)/2 - sqrt((I_y - I_z)^2/4 + I_yz^2)
'Angle of principal axis
α_1 = atan((I_y - I_1)/I_yz)
'Polar moment of area
I_x = I_y + I_z
'Radii of gyration
r_y = sqrt(I_y/A)
r_z = sqrt(I_z/A)
r_1 = sqr(I_1/A)
r_2 = sqr(I_2/A)
r_x = sqrt(I_x/A)
